  - chat,ghat are EXPLICIT singular series for a FIXED bounded speed set (max 84).
  - The N-sum is absolutely convergent with elementary 1/N^2 tails (BV/indicator TV).
  - There is NO unbounded family of moduli to average over => the BV/EH 'level of
    distribution' machinery has nothing to act on.  The only equidistribution used is
    orthogonality of characters on a FIXED cyclic group (ahat supported on rZ): elementary.
  - DIAGONAL (single-relation, divisor sum over r|14N) carries most of the L1 mass;
    OFF-DIAGONAL is a geometrically smaller absolutely-summable correction.
  => EH is NOT needed.  Not even BV.  The uniform bound is elementary harmonic analysis.
